Batch 5b of ADR-0064 (shared call resolution): Perl, Ruby, Lua and Go report calls with facts and hand over a per-file import table; the shared linkers decide. Python was in this batch and is pulled into its own pull request (below).

## What changes for a reader of a map

In these four languages a call is no longer bound because some declaration in the repository has its name. It is bound by what the language's own rule says (the caller's package or scope, an import, the receiver's type), or it is left unresolved.

