## The name step

On for Lua only, with a screen of the standard library, LuaJIT and OpenResty names: 411 binds, all calls on a receiver; of 15 read, 12 right, 2 wrong (methods of a heap library's and the Postgres client's objects), 1 not decidable. Off for Ruby (measured on: 7 right of 15; a Rails model's columns and associations) and Go (12 right of 15; standard-library methods its screen does not hold); it does nothing for Perl. The Ruby and Lua screens were written without the documentation at hand (its sites are not on the network allowlist) and are not checked against it.

## Shared-layer changes (each with a test that fails without it)

- A module of the file kind may be a directory (Go's package): the files directly in it; the caller's own directory is a scope.
- A method declared outside its type's file belongs to the type its declared name says (it went to the first type of that short name in the run). On caddy: 16 typed calls now bound, 2 wrong binds gone, 4 wrong `dispatches_to` edges gone and 3 right ones new.
- Perl and Lua are declared inputs of the inherited-calls linker; a test derives that from who builds an import table.

## What must not change

Ten repositories of languages outside the batch (JavaScript / TypeScript, Rust, Java, Kotlin, C#, PHP, and three Python trees): identical in every edge and symbol. In the four languages: no declared symbol changed but for Perl's new `qualified_name` (no id, no stable id moved); edges other than calls identical except the seven `dispatches_to` edges above.

## One verify-claims reason changes

Go's adapter types a package variable from its declaration, so `db.Exec(v)` on `var db *sql.DB` now names `database/sql`. A "never reaches a database" claim on such a program is still not confirmed, but the stated reason is the module the I/O catalogue cannot classify, where it was "Go has no sink in the database zone". Found by the pre-PR run; both cases are pinned.

## Python

Its adapter's first round lost 176 resolved calls on this repository's own map; 15 of 15 read were right before. Scripts reach `scripts/lib` through `sys.path.insert`, which the new exact module lookup did not read, and the scheduled gates and test selection of this repository read those edges. It gets a second round and its own pull request.

## Still wrong or lost, to be filed after the merge (each with its count)

Perl's indirect-object `throw Class(..)` (19 right edges lost) and its methods being invisible to the linkers; Go receivers that are range variables, interface-method results or two-value returns, and a hint that cannot name a type of a package the caller does not import; Lua tables with no type symbol (232 open stubs); Ruby `attr_reader` sends to `self` (53); the name step's fall-through for a module qualifier, which misbound Lua 9 times of 10 before its table stopped handing bindings over.

## Not checked

No repository outside the 21 was run. The moved edges outside the samples were not read. Confidence values, slices, dead-code and taint output beyond the existing tests were not compared. One run per tree: analysis time is not measured.
